5.30.m:
Dharma said:
‘This one had relations with his friend's wife who trusted him;
therefore, I have cooked him on an iron stake for ten thousand years.

Dharma said:
Viṣṇu was not worshipped by these, nor were his stories heard by them;
how indeed can there be release from hell for evil-doers?

5.31.m:
Ṛtaṃbhara said:
"O master, at your command I remained in the forest guarding the cow;
coming from somewhere unseen, a lion killed her.
